  "body": "## What changed\r\n\r\n- A STEP import now examines each body of the finished mesh (a body is a connected set of facets). A body that is closed, manifold, consistently wound and has a clearly negative signed volume is wound inward. The importer reverses each facet of that body, so the body turns outward.\r\n- The verdict uses `pick::winding::winding_of`. The face picks use the same test. Thus the importer and the picks agree on what \"inward\" means.\r\n- The importer does not change an open body (a lone face, a shell with a gap), a non-manifold body, a body with mixed winding or a body with no volume.\r\n- The import tells the user about the change. `Graded::notes` and `ImportModel::notes` are new. The note goes to the MCP and script `import` result (`notes`) and to the status line.\r\n- New module: `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_outward.rs`. `step.rs` does not change.\r\n\r\n## Overlap\r\n\r\n- PR #1576 adds the same `notes` plumbing for its flipped faces: `Graded`, `ImportModel`, `v_import`, `cam.d.ts`, `script/mod.rs`, the MCP description and the status line in `ui/src/state.rs`. Where possible, the code lines here are the same as the lines in #1576. The second PR to merge must keep one copy of the plumbing. In `parse_model_graded_within`, it must keep both note sources (the #1576 face notes and the `step_outward` note).\r\n- PR #1638 changes `step.rs` and the module list in `import/mod.rs`. This PR does not change `step.rs`. It adds `mod step_outward;` at a different line of the module list.\r\n\r\n## How tested\r\n\r\n- `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_outward_tests.rs` (unit): an outward cube, an inward cube, two bodies with one inward, a lone curved face (both windings) and a mixed cube.\r\n- `crates/app/tests/import_step_outward.rs`:\r\n  - `an_inward_closed_box_is_turned_outward_and_said`: `box.step` with all senses reversed imports with the same positive volume as the plain box, and with one note.\r\n  - `a_lone_curved_face_is_left_alone`: the B-spline face of `bspline_dome.step` alone in an `OPEN_SHELL`, in both windings. No note, and each keeps its own winding.\r\n  - `the_mcp_import_result_carries_the_note`: the MCP `import_model` result has `notes` for the inward box and no `notes` for the plain box.\r\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/import_outward.rs`: `an_inward_solid_is_turned_and_said_on_the_status_line`.\r\n- All of the tests above pass on head 8926917.\r\n- These suites also pass: the `camcraft-app` lib tests that match `import`, and `import_step_guard`, `mcp`, `model_fidelity`, `scripting`, `step_budget`, `step_chord_units`, `step_fidelity`, `step_nesting`, ui `models` and ui `fixtures`.\r\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings` is clean.\r\n\r\n## Not exercised\r\n\r\n- The local part `step-block-371.step` from the issue. It is not in the repository.\r\n- An STL or OBJ body that is wound inward. This PR does not change STL or OBJ import.\r\n- The full quick-gate list (all MCP, script and ui suites that the gate map names) and the batch tier.\r\n\r\nChangelog: A closed STEP solid that the file winds inward now imports turned outward, and the import says so in its notes and on the status line (#1617).\r\n\r\nEffort: high (not escalated).\r\n\r\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\r\n\r\nFixes #1617\r\n",
